STATE OF LOC NATION CENTRAL BANK
STATE OF LOC NATION GLOBAL PUBLIC BENEFIT CORPORATION
AMENDMENT NO. SOLN-CB-AMEND-2026-0831-001
AMENDMENT TO RESOLUTION NO. SOLN-CB-RES-2026-0831-001 RATIFYING A
4,000,000,000 LND SUPPLEMENTAL AUTHORIZED RESERVE AND ESTABLISHING A
TOTAL AUTHORIZED OPENING ISSUANCE OF 4,400,000,000 LND
Adoption Date: August 31, 2026
Effective Date: August 31, 2026
Functional Currency: Loc Nation Dollar
Ledger Precision: Two decimal places
Smallest Ledger Denomination: One LND cent
Authorized Reporting Rate: 1 LND = 750 USD equivalent
WHEREAS, Resolution No. SOLN-CB-RES-2026-0831-001 authorized an original opening
issuance of 400,000,000.00 LND;
WHEREAS, the original 400,000,000.00 LND allocation schedule supports economic relief,
infrastructure, education and health, sovereign reserves, trade and foreign-exchange programs,
credit-union participation, business-readiness training, justice initiatives, and disaster-relief
programs;
WHEREAS, the SOLN issuance wallet presently records 440,000,000,000 LND cents, equal to
4,400,000,000.00 LND;
WHEREAS, the State of Loc Nation Central Bank has determined that the additional
4,000,000,000.00 LND shall be retained and ratified as a supplemental authorized reserve;
NOW, THEREFORE, BE IT RESOLVED:
SECTION 1. RATIFICATION OF SUPPLEMENTAL ISSUANCE
The State of Loc Nation Central Bank hereby ratifies the existing supplemental issuance of:
4,000,000,000.00 LND
The corresponding ledger amount is:
400,000,000,000 LND cents
The supplemental amount is designated as the SOLN Supplemental Authorized Reserve.
SECTION 2. TOTAL AUTHORIZED OPENING ISSUANCE
OFFICIAL AMENDMENT REFERENCE:
SOLN-CB-AMEND-2026-0831-001
Resolution No. SOLN-CB-RES-2026-0831-001 is amended so that the total authorized opening
issuance is:
4,400,000,000.00 LND
The corresponding ledger amount is:
440,000,000,000 LND cents
At the adopted reporting rate of 1 LND to 750 USD equivalent, the total stated value is:
3,300,000,000,000.00 USD equivalent
SECTION 3. ORIGINAL ALLOCATION SCHEDULE PRESERVED
The original 400,000,000.00 LND allocation schedule remains unchanged:
1. Economic Relief Programs — 100,000,000.00 LND;
2. Infrastructure Programs — 120,000,000.00 LND;
3. Education and Health Programs — 60,000,000.00 LND;
4. Sovereign Reserve — 80,000,000.00 LND;
5. Trade and Foreign-Exchange Programs — 20,000,000.00 LND; and
6. Credit-Union Issuance and Participation Programs — 20,000,000.00 LND.
The LND Accrual Readiness Training Initiative, Nolan Xavier Wells Justice Pledge, and
Gary–Northwest Indiana–Illinois Emergency Disaster-Relief Pledge remain governed by the
original allocation schedule.
SECTION 4. SUPPLEMENTAL AUTHORIZED RESERVE
The additional 4,000,000,000.00 LND shall remain classified as a supplemental authorized
reserve until allocated by a subsequently adopted resolution, order, program authorization,
approved budget, or other governing instrument.
The supplemental reserve may support authorized:
1. Economic-development programs;
2. Restitution programs;
3. Community investment;
4. Infrastructure;
5. Education and health;
6. Emergency and disaster relief;
7. Business development and accrual readiness;
8. Housing and community stabilization;
9. Trade and foreign-exchange operations;
10. Credit-union participation;
OFFICIAL AMENDMENT REFERENCE:
SOLN-CB-AMEND-2026-0831-001
11. Institutional partnerships;
12. Humanitarian programs;
13. Justice-related programs; and
14. Other programs approved by SOLN.
SECTION 5. NO DUPLICATE POSTING
This Amendment ratifies an amount already reflected in WALLET-LND-ISSUANCE.
Implementation of this Amendment shall not:
1. Add another 4,000,000,000.00 LND to the wallet;
2. Duplicate the existing journal entry;
3. Duplicate the issuance authorization; or
4. Increase the total above 4,400,000,000.00 LND.
The implementation function shall reclassify the existing supplemental authorization, attach this
Amendment’s reference, and create an audit record without changing the wallet balance.
SECTION 6. LEDGER AND AUTHORIZATION REFERENCES
The original 400,000,000.00 LND remains governed by:
SOLN-CB-RES-2026-0831-001
The supplemental 4,000,000,000.00 LND reserve is governed by:
SOLN-CB-AMEND-2026-0831-001
The total authorized issuance is:
4,400,000,000.00 LND
440,000,000,000 LND cents
SECTION 7. FINANCIAL REPORTING
The issuance register, trial balance, balance sheet, reserve report, allocation report, and audit
log shall separately identify:
1. Original program allocations — 400,000,000.00 LND;
2. Supplemental authorized reserve — 4,000,000,000.00 LND; and
3. Total authorized opening issuance — 4,400,000,000.00 LND.
USD-equivalent amounts shall be presented separately using the adopted reporting rate.
SECTION 8. MAKER-CHECKER AND DISTRIBUTION CONTROLS
OFFICIAL AMENDMENT REFERENCE:
SOLN-CB-AMEND-2026-0831-001
No amount from the supplemental reserve shall be transferred or distributed without:
1. A governing allocation or program authorization;
2. An identified source and destination wallet;
3. A unique transaction identifier;
4. A maker submission;
5. Separate checker approval;
6. Source-balance validation;
7. Balanced journal entries;
8. Updated wallet balances; and
9. A complete audit record.
SECTION 9. CONTINUING EFFECT
Except as amended by this instrument, all provisions of Resolution No.
SOLN-CB-RES-2026-0831-001 remain in effect.
SECTION 10. EFFECTIVE DATE
This Amendment is adopted and effective on August 31, 2026.
